      <data key="d10">[{"path": "primary_sources/m04/SFP-M04_v0.2.tex", "start": 80, "end": 139, "role": "statement", "name": "SFP-M04_v0.2.tex", "excerpt": "80: \\section{Complete convex coordinates and normalization}\\label{sec:normal}\n81: Fix $X\\ge0$ with $c=X\\one&gt;0$, let $x=X^T\\one$, and fix a row-stochastic $K\\times N$ matrix $B$. The prescribed effective routing is $A=\\diag(c)^{-1}X$.\n82: \\begin{theorem}[Complete regular fiber]\\label{thm:fiber}\n83: The space of output-regular networks with these $c,A,B$ is homeomorphic to the nonempty convex set\n84: \\begin{equation}\\label{eq:domain}\n85:  \\mathcal D_B=\\{M=M^T\\succ0: M_{k\\ell}\\le0\\ (k\\ne\\ell),\\ MB\\ge0\\}.\n86: \\end{equation}\n87: The forward coordinate is $M=\\diag(z)Q\\diag(z)$. Its inverse is\n88: \\begin{align}\\label{eq:inverse}\n89:  r&amp;=\\one+M^{-1}x,\\qquad R=\\diag(r),\\nonumber\\\\\n90:  U&amp;=XR,\\qquad V=RMB,\\qquad\n91:  W_{k\\ell}=-r_kM_{k\\ell}r_\\ell\\ (k\\ne\\ell),\\quad W_{kk}=0.\n92: \\end{align}\n93: Every such network has $C=XB$. In particular, the fixed-effective-factor fiber is contractible.\n94: \\end{theorem}\n95: \\begin{proof}\n96: Positive definite matrices form a convex cone; the remaining restrictions in \\eqref{eq:domain} are linear. Positive diagonal matrices belong to $\\mathcal D_B$, establishing nonemptiness. Also $M\\one=MB\\one\\ge0$. The inverse-positivity argument of Lemma~\\ref{lem:projection} gives $r\\ge\\one$, so \\eqref{eq:inverse} gives finite nonnegative conductances and symmetric $W$.\n97: \n98: The off-diagonals of $RMR$ equal $-W$. Its row sums satisfy\n99: \\begin{equation}\\label{eq:rowsum}\n… Полный диапазон см. в источнике."}]</data>
