    <node id="m04_safe_probe">
      <data key="d0">Физический зонд устраняет адресную неизвестность без резерва</data>
      <data key="d1">На специальном полном DtN-слое одна общая политика безопасно идентифицирует адреса, возвращает реальные проводимости и калибрует функцию при исходной ширине N.</data>
      <data key="d2">theorem</data>
      <data key="d3">established</data>
      <data key="d4">electrical</data>
      <data key="d5">Наблюдение и доступ</data>
      <data key="d6">["Доступно адресное относительное управление", "Измеряется полный DtN", "Точная диагностика"]</data>
      <data key="d7">["Интерфейс отличается от M03; нельзя приписать исчезновение накладного слота только субстрату", "Не оптимизировано число/время проб"]</data>
      <data key="d8">Результат заявлен в канонической рукописи; мировой приоритет этим извлечением не проверен.</data>
      <data key="d9">proof_spot_checked</data>
      <data key="d10">[{"path": "primary_sources/m04/SFP-M04_v0.2.tex", "start": 243, "end": 272, "role": "statement", "name": "SFP-M04_v0.2.tex", "excerpt": "243: \\section{Safe probing, return, and calibration}\\label{sec:probe}\n244: The controller initially knows the network belongs to the \\emph{entire} fiber \\eqref{eq:LambdaStar}, and knows $G_{\\rm ref},\\varepsilon,g_0,G_{\\rm out}$ and the addressed internal ports. It does not read the individual conductances or the unknown permutation. It may synchronously multiply all $U$ edges entering one chosen internal address and all its $V$ edges by specified relative factors. After a positive-duration command it observes the exact full DtN. Once addresses are identified, individual input conductances can be adjusted for calibration. The whole continuous command must satisfy \\eqref{eq:fit}, with $c=g_0\\one$ fixed. Only $C$ is protected; $\\Lambda_{LL}$ may change. An observation-based policy chooses each next continuous command from its observation and command history and must be safe and successful for every compatible initial realization. Its peak is the worst-case number of available internal vertices; the observation-based minimum is taken over these common policies. The known-realization minimum allows the initial conductances to be known.\n245: \n246: \\begin{proposition}[One policy for the full fiber]\\label{prop:probe}\n247: Under this interface, the initially unfinished terminal $C=g_0P$ is achievable for every network in \\eqref{eq:LambdaStar} with peak $N$. Thus the known-realization and observation-based minimum peaks both equal $N$.\n248: \\end{proposition}\n249: \\begin{proof}\n250: At address $k$, choose a known continuous scalar $q(t)&gt;g_0$, with $q(0)=G_{\\rm out}$ and a final value different from $G_{\\rm out}$. Execute\n251: \\begin{align}\\label{eq:probe}\n252:  U_{\\cdot k}(t)&amp;=\\frac{q(t)(G_{\\rm out}-g_0)}{G_{\\rm out}(q(t)-g_0)}U_{\\cdot k}(0),\\nonumber\\\\\n253:  V_{k\\cdot}(t)&amp;=\\frac{q(t)}{G_{\\rm out}}V_{k\\cdot}(0).\n254: \\end{align}\n255: These relative coefficients are known before the command and are independent of $j=\\sigma(k)$. The star now has\n256: \\[\n257:  U_{\\cdot k}(t)=\\frac{g_0q(t)}{q(t)-g_0}a_j,\\quad\n258:  V_{k\\cdot}(t)=q(t)e_j^T,\\quad Q_{kk}(t)=\\frac{q(t)^2}{q(t)-g_0}.\n259: \\]\n260: Its cross contribution is exactly $g_0a_je_j^T$ and its output contribution is $g_0e_je_j^T$. Therefore $C,c,\\Lambda_{RR}$ stay unchanged for the entire probe, including states on the initial error boundary. The measured change is\n261: \\begin{equation}\\label{eq:signal}\n262:  \\Delta\\Lambda_{LL}=g_0^2\\left(\\frac1{q-g_0}-\\frac1{G_{\\rm out}-g_0}\\right)K_j.\n… Полный диапазон см. в источнике."}]</data>
