      <data key="d5">История и организация обучения</data>
      <data key="d6">["Регулярный градиентный learner", "Доступны знакопеременные цели, реализующие подъёмы", "Малый цикл и фиксированное малое положительное время"]</data>
      <data key="d7">["Ненулевое Ω само не означает память", "Нет универсально полезной ориентации"]</data>
      <data key="d8">Операционное применение известной геометрической фазы; рукопись различает механизм и известный аппарат.</data>
      <data key="d9">proof_spot_checked</data>
      <data key="d10">[{"path": "primary_sources/m05/sections/mechanism.tex", "start": 4, "end": 52, "role": "statement", "name": "mechanism.tex", "excerpt": "4: \\subsection{Closed functional cycles and hidden displacement}\n5: Define the horizontal lifts of the output coordinates and their brackets by\n6: \\begin{equation}\n7:  L_a=J^\\top K^{-1}e_a,\\qquad\n8:  \\Omega_{ab}=[L_a,L_b]=\\dd L_b[L_a]-\\dd L_a[L_b].\n9:  \\label{eq:bracket}\n10: \\end{equation}\n11: Since $JL_a=e_a$, differentiation and symmetry of $\\dd^2C$ give $J\\Omega_{ab}=0$. Thus $\\Omega_{ab}$ is tangent to the functional level set. The geometric phase generated by a closed visible path is standard \\cite{kelly1995}; its operational action on later learning is the issue here.\n12: \n13: Following $+L_a,+L_b,-L_a,-L_b$ for side duration $s$ defines $H_+(s,x)$. The reversed traversal $+L_b,+L_a,-L_b,-L_a$ defines $H_-(s,x)$. All durations are positive. Each lift changes precisely its designated output coordinate, so both paths return the full $C$ exactly. Their endpoints satisfy\n14: \\begin{align}\n15:  H_\\pm(s,x)&amp;=x\\pm s^2\\Omega_{ab}(x)+O(s^3),\\label{eq:cycle}\\\\\n16:  K(H_\\pm(s,x))&amp;=K(x)\\pm s^2\\Action_{ab}(x)+O(s^3),\n17:  \\qquad \\Action_{ab}=\\dd K[\\Omega_{ab}].\\label{eq:action}\n18: \\end{align}\n19: The lift with velocity $+L_a$ is generated through \\eqref{eq:gradient} by the goal $q=C+K^{-1}e_a$, and the negative lift by $q=C-K^{-1}e_a$. This uses a known-model target planner, not an additional parameter actuator. The finite neural construction in Appendix~\\ref{app:compiler} approximates these arcs with ordinary constant targets and pays for the approximation.\n20: \n21: \\subsection{Action on a common next episode}\n22: \\begin{theorem}[Sufficient condition for finite future distinction]\n23: \\label{thm:mechanism}\n… Полный диапазон см. в источнике."}]</data>
      <data key="d11">История действует через изменение будущего оператора обучения</data>
