      <data key="d10">[{"path": "primary_sources/m06/sections/03_results.tex", "start": 1, "end": 21, "role": "statement", "name": "03_results.tex", "excerpt": "1: \\section{Resource bounds}\\label{sec:results}\n2: \\begin{theorem}[Sharp finite-accuracy resource law]\\label{thm:main}\n3: There exist constants $c,C,\\del_0&gt;0$, depending only on the fixed model in \\cref{sec:model}, such that for every $N\\ge2$ and $0&lt;\\del\\le\\del_0$, with $L_\\del=1+\\log(1/\\del)$,\n4: \\begin{equation}\\label{eq:main-law}\n5:  c\\min\\{N,L_\\del^2\\}\n6:  \\le m_{\\mathrm{free}}(N,\\del)\n7:  \\le m_{\\mathrm{all}}(N,\\del)\n8:  \\le m_{\\mathrm{star}}(N,\\del)\n9:  \\le C\\min\\{N,L_\\del^2\\}.\n10: \\end{equation}\n11: The upper bound is attained by a fixed parallel star ensemble with a single $C^\\infty$ initialization map and strictly positive conductances. The lower bound allows discontinuous, source-dependent choices of topology and initialization.\n12: \\end{theorem}\n13: \n14: \\begin{corollary}[Constant-factor comparison of topologies]\\label{cor:topology}\n15: For the same $N$ and $\\del$ as in \\cref{thm:main},\n16: \\begin{equation}\\label{eq:constant-comparison}\n17:  m_{\\mathrm{star}}(N,\\del)\n18:  \\le (C/c)\\,m_{\\mathrm{free}}(N,\\del).\n19: \\end{equation}\n20: \\end{corollary}\n… Полный диапазон см. в источнике."}]</data>
