      <data key="d10">[{"path": "primary_sources/m06/sections/04_sensitivity.tex", "start": 4, "end": 69, "role": "statement", "name": "04_sensitivity.tex", "excerpt": "4: \\begin{lemma}[Uniform electrical and learning sensitivity]\\label{lem:physical-lip}\n5: For every admissible graph $H$, and all positive initial states $g,g'$ on $H$ with $\\sum g_e,\\sum g'_e\\le1$,\n6: \\begin{equation}\\label{eq:physical-lip}\n7:  \\norm{\\cR_H(g)-\\cR_H(g')}_\\infty\n8:  \\le K_0\\norm{\\sqrt g-\\sqrt{g'}}_2,\n9:  \\qquad K_0=\\sqrt7\\,e^{105/8}.\n10: \\end{equation}\n11: The constant is independent of $m$, topology, and the smallest conductance.\n12: \\end{lemma}\n13: \\begin{proof}\n14: Let $B_I$ consist of the interior columns of the incidence matrix, and set $D=\\diag(\\sqrt g)$ and $A=B_I^\\top D^2B_I$. If $B_I$ is empty the following projection is zero. Otherwise $A$ is positive definite and\n15: \\[\n16:  \\Pi=DB_I A^{-1}B_I^\\top D\n17: \\]\n18: is an orthogonal projector. Its bound $\\norm{\\Pi}_{2\\to2}\\le1$ therefore holds uniformly, including for poorly conditioned $A$.\n19: \n20: For a boundary basis voltage $e_a$, let $u^a$ be its harmonic extension and $t^a=Bu^a$ the vector of edge voltage drops. The discrete maximum principle gives $|t_e^a|\\le1$. Differentiating the stationary Dirichlet energy with respect to an edge conductance gives, for $a\\ne b$,\n21: \\begin{equation}\\label{eq:sensitivity-edge}\n22:  \\partial_{g_e} C_{ab}(g)=-t_e^a t_e^b.\n23: \\end{equation}\n… Полный диапазон см. в источнике."}]</data>
      <data key="d11">Равномерная чувствительность ограничивает все топологии</data>
