      <data key="d9">primary_statement_checked</data>
      <data key="d10">[{"path": "WEAK_TASK_LEARNING_20261029/JPA_ADAPTATION_20261105/source/sections/02_model_results.tex", "start": 59, "end": 75, "role": "statement", "name": "02_model_results.tex", "excerpt": "59: \\subsection{Full matrix programming and subsequent weak learning}\n60: \\begin{theorem}[Response-matrix programming through teaching]\\label{thm:main}\n61: For every finite $L\\ge2$ there is an open dense, scale-invariant set $\\mathcal R_L\\subset\\R_{&gt;0}^{3L}$, dense on each positive $Q$-level, with these properties.\n62: \n63: For every $g_0\\in\\mathcal R_L$ and every neighborhood $U$ of $g_0$ on its $Q$-level, there is a neighborhood $\\mathcal W$ of zero in $\\Sym_2$ such that each $S\\in\\mathcal W$ is attained by a finite-duration teaching trajectory contained in $U$ with\n64: \\begin{equation}\\label{eq:endpoint}\n65:  g(0)=g_0,\\quad \\phi(g(T_p))=\\phi(g_0),\\quad\n66:  K(g(T_p))=K(g_0)+S.\n67: \\end{equation}\n68: The control amplitude can respect any specified positive bound, with duration allowed to change, and the targets can remain in $(0,1)^2$.\n69: \n70: For any such prepared endpoint $g_1$ and any fixed $H&lt;\\infty$, subsequent squared-error teaching toward $y=\\phi_0+h$ from either $g_k$, $k=0,1$, satisfies\n71: \\begin{equation}\\label{eq:generalresponse}\n72:  \\phi(g_k(t;h))-(\\phi_0+h)=-e^{-K_kt}h+O(\\|h\\|^2),\n73:  \\qquad K_1=K_0+S,\n74: \\end{equation}\n75: uniformly for $0\\le t\\le H$ and all directions of sufficiently small $h$."}]</data>
      <data key="d11">Полная матрица будущего отклика программируема обучением</data>
      <data key="d12">learning</data>
      <data key="d13">-280.0</data>
      <data key="d14">-840.0</data>
