      <data key="d3">conditional</data>
      <data key="d4">abstract</data>
      <data key="d5">Наблюдение и доступ</data>
      <data key="d6">["Условия P,O,S", "Общая область и шумовое окно", "Диагностика и управление могут чередоваться"]</data>
      <data key="d7">["За пределами окна границы не совпадают", "Реализация p=2,q=3,r=3 — отдельный физический результат"]</data>
      <data key="d8">Результат заявлен в канонической рукописи; мировой приоритет этим извлечением не проверен.</data>
      <data key="d9">primary_statement_checked</data>
      <data key="d10">[{"path": "SFP_M09_OBSERVATION_ACCESS_20261102/SICON_SUBMISSION_PREPARATION_20261102/SOURCE/manuscript/conditions.tex", "start": 45, "end": 83, "role": "statement", "name": "conditions.tex", "excerpt": "45: \\begin{theorem}[Full-time access bound]\\label{thm:general}\n46: Under P, O, and S, define\n47: \\[\n48:  a_\\delta(s)=\n49:  \\begin{cases}\n50:  \\min\\{(\\delta/s)^{1/p},\\delta^{1/q}\\},&amp;s&gt;0,\\\\\n51:  \\delta^{1/q},&amp;s\\le0 .\n52:  \\end{cases}\n53: \\]\n54: The informed cost is $\\orac(s)\\asymp a_\\delta(s)/U$. Every correct causal policy satisfies, for $s&gt;0$,\n55: \\begin{equation}\\label{eq:lower}\n56:  \\sup_e UT_\\pi(s,e)\\ge\n57:  c\\max\\left\\{a_\\delta(s),\n58:        \\min\\left[\\delta^{1/q},(\\sigma/s)^{1/r}\\right]\\right\\}.\n59: \\end{equation}\n60: There exists one common policy with\n61: \\begin{equation}\\label{eq:upper}\n62:  \\sup_e UT_\\pi(s,e)\\le\n63:  C\\left[a_\\delta(s)+\n64:     \\left(\\frac{\\sigma a_\\delta(s)^p}{\\delta}\\right)^{1/r}\\right]\n… Полный диапазон см. в источнике."}, {"path": "SFP_M09_OBSERVATION_ACCESS_20261102/SICON_SUBMISSION_PREPARATION_20261102/SOURCE/manuscript/conditions.tex", "start": 4, "end": 43, "role": "assumptions", "name": "conditions.tex", "excerpt": "4: Consider a smooth driftless system\n5: \\[\n6:  \\dot x=\\sum_{i=1}^d u_iY_i(x),\\qquad \\norm{u}_1\\le U,\n7: \\]\n8: on an open admissible domain. A known smooth one-parameter family $x_s$, $|s|\\le s_0\\le1$, has common $C(x_s)=C_0$ and common symmetric target matrix $F(x_s)=F_0$. Observation, execution, policies, and costs have the contract of Section~\\ref{sec:model}, with $F$ replacing $K$. All derivative and remainder bounds below are uniform on a common relatively compact neighborhood. Set $\\tau=UT$.\n9: \n10: \\paragraph{P: physical bounds and finite programs.}\n11: For integers $2\\le p&lt;q$, every sufficiently short successful trajectory satisfies\n12: \\begin{equation}\\label{eq:P}\n13:  \\delta\\le B(s_+\\tau^p+\\tau^q+\\kappa\\delta),\\qquad\n14:  s_+=\\max(s,0),\\qquad B\\kappa&lt;\\tfrac12.\n15: \\end{equation}\n16: There are two model-computable nominal programs of time at most $Bh/U$, each returning $C$ exactly at its nominal state, such that\n17: \\begin{equation}\\label{eq:programs}\n18:  \\lambda_{\\min}(\\Delta F_p)\\ge as h^p-bh^q\\quad(s&gt;0),\n19:  \\qquad\n20:  \\lambda_{\\min}(\\Delta F_q)\\ge ah^q-bh^{q+1}\n21:  \\quad(|s|\\le s_0).\n22: \\end{equation}\n23: A positive normalized time is required to exit the smaller common neighborhood.\n… Полный диапазон см. в источнике."}]</data>
