    <node id="m09_noise_threshold">
      <data key="d0">Шум меньше задачи всё равно уничтожает быстрый масштаб</data>
      <data key="d1">В физическом классе порог ограниченного проигрыша знающему контроллеру σ*=δ^(3/2)/sqrt(s); при σ=δ^(5/4) и фиксированном s относительная потеря времени расходится как δ^(-1/12), хотя σ/δ→0.</data>
      <data key="d2">counterexample</data>
      <data key="d3">established</data>
      <data key="d4">electrical</data>
      <data key="d5">Наблюдение и доступ</data>
      <data key="d6">["Фиксированная нормировка единиц", "Быстрый локальный режим и окно шума"]</data>
      <data key="d7">["Не универсальный шумовой порог всех систем"]</data>
      <data key="d8">Результат заявлен в канонической рукописи; мировой приоритет этим извлечением не проверен.</data>
      <data key="d9">proof_spot_checked</data>
      <data key="d10">[{"path": "SFP_M09_OBSERVATION_ACCESS_20261102/SICON_SUBMISSION_PREPARATION_20261102/SOURCE/manuscript/main_result.tex", "start": 39, "end": 61, "role": "statement", "name": "main_result.tex", "excerpt": "39: The noise scale for retaining a bounded time ratio to the informed controller is\n40: \\begin{equation}\\label{eq:threshold}\n41:  \\sigma_*(s,\\delta)=\\frac{\\delta^{3/2}}{\\sqrt{s}}.\n42: \\end{equation}\n43: For each fixed $R$, one common policy has bounded ratio when $\\sigma\\le R\\sigma_*$. If $\\sigma/\\sigma_*\\to\\infty$ while $\\delta/s^3\\to0$, every correct policy has unbounded worst-case ratio. The latter conclusion is a lower bound and does not extend the matched formula beyond \\eqref{eq:window}.\n44: \\end{theorem}\n45: \n46: The constructive and informational parts of the theorem are distinct. The finite certificate in Appendix~\\ref{app:certificate} establishes an accessible family with the stated jets and cubic channel. Sections~\\ref{sec:physical}--\\ref{sec:bounds} explain why these premises imply the cost law. No numerical working radius or execution schedule for a noisy device is asserted.\n47: \n48: \\begin{corollary}[Noise smaller than the task can still cost an unbounded factor]\\label{cor:smallnoise}\n49: Fix a sufficiently small $s&gt;0$ and use the fixed voltage and conductance normalization of the model. For $\\sigma=\\delta^{5/4}$,\n50: \\[\n51:  \\orac(s)\\asymp\\frac{\\delta^{1/2}}U,\\qquad\n52:  \\obs(s,\\delta,\\sigma)\\asymp\\frac{\\delta^{5/12}}U,\\qquad\n53:  \\frac{\\obs}{\\orac}\\asymp\\delta^{-1/12}\\longrightarrow\\infty.\n54: \\]\n55: Nevertheless, $\\sigma/\\delta\\to0$, and $\\delta^{5/12}=o(\\delta^{1/3})$.\n56: \\end{corollary}\n57: \\begin{proof}\n58: For fixed $s$, \\eqref{eq:window} and the fast-regime condition hold for small enough $\\delta$. Substitute $\\sigma=\\delta^{5/4}$ in \\eqref{eq:introprice}; its observation term dominates its informed term.\n… Полный диапазон см. в источнике."}]</data>
