      <data key="d10">[{"path": "primary_sources/m10/sections/06_lower_limits.tex", "start": 30, "end": 90, "role": "statement", "name": "06_lower_limits.tex", "excerpt": "30: \\begin{lemma}[Blind short-time barrier]\\label{lem:blind}\n31: Fix $0&lt;s_*\\le s_0$. If $\\delta&gt;\\rho^2$, no single record of sufficiently\n32: small length $\\ell\\le\\min(1,\\sqrt{s_*/2})$ can satisfy\n33: $\\Delta K_C\\succeq\\delta I_2$ and $\\norm C\\le\\rho$ at both starts $a_{\\pm s_*}$.\n34: \\end{lemma}\n35: \\begin{proof}\n36: The identity $\\norm{C(q,z)}^2=(1+z^2)\\norm q^2$ implies\n37: $s_*\\norm p\\le\\rho$ if both endpoints meet the return bound.\n38: Since $|z|\\le s_*|r|$ for the stated short records,\n39: \\[\n40:  \\min\\{(z+s_*r)^2,(z-s_*r)^2\\}\n41:  \\le s_*^2r^2=s_*^2+s_*^2\\norm p^2\\le s_*^2+\\rho^2.\n42: \\]\n43: The smaller eigenvalue of each own learning increment is exactly\n44: $(z\\pm s_*r)^2-s_*^2$. At least one is at most $\\rho^2&lt;\\delta$.\n45: \\end{proof}\n46: \n47: \\subsection{One shared reading is insufficient even after a chosen prelude}\n48: For this lower bound take the product prior containing the full $s$ interval,\n49: the square $\\theta\\in[1,6/5]^2$, and the balanced physical port for every $\\theta$.\n… Полный диапазон см. в источнике."}]</data>
      <data key="d11">Два чтения имеют доказанную функциональную работу</data>
